From 0c15dd27eff00b8db0d8578d172354187682d5f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:59:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The cameraman films a fight from outside it (WOW_SPECTATE)
 (patch 0088)

`WOW_SPECTATE=<subject>,<hero>[,<shot>]` makes this client Basin Battle's cameraman: its camera
leaves its own body (free-fly, the body hidden, the sound heard at the camera) and keeps the named
creature (a boss) and player (the hero) in view, framed by the shot:

- `duel` (the default): a three-quarter side view from the hero's side, 10 to 14 yd out.
- `low`: 20 yd out and low, for a big body (the Shredder).
- `high`: 45 to 60 degrees up, so a ground hazard's edge shows.

The distance grows past the shot's range only when the two would not fit. When either is hidden
from the camera for more than 0.3 s, by the world (the camera's own collision sweep) or by another
body standing on the line, the camera cuts to the shot's next position whose view of both is
clear: the other side, square to the side, behind, then the same higher. Otherwise the eye follows
the fight smoothly, and the fight's axis turns slowly, so the camera doesn't whip round as the two
circle. With no subject, or none in sight, it frames the hero alone, looking past them the way
they face; with the hero gone for 3 s (a world change) it goes back to the body.

The eye is written after `control` and the camera shake, each frame, so a teleport of the body or
a shake never moves it. `fly_free` hides the body while a cameraman has the eye (`filming` on the
rig), where it used to keep it opaque. Unset: nothing changes.

The server keeps the cameraman's hero out of the fight and unseen (Basin Battle's `.es watch`);
the visual check runs it as a second client beside the hero's (docs/visual-check.md there).
